# Compiled binaries. NOTHING built from this repo belongs in git.
#
# `go build ./cmd/agent` writes ./agent -- the package name, in the working
# directory -- and that is how a 9 MB macOS binary and an 8 MB Windows one were
# committed once. The anchored entries below name every binary a bare `go build`
# of this repo's own commands can drop at the root.
#
# There is deliberately no `/api` entry: a tracked api/ directory lives there
# (the OpenAPI contract), so `go build ./cmd/api` cannot overwrite it, and an
# ignore rule with that name would hide the contract instead.
#
# scripts/check-no-binaries.sh enforces the rule rather than trusting this list,
# because the next artifact will have a name nobody predicted.
/agent
/migrations-drift-check
/openapi-yaml
*.exe
*.dll
*.dylib
*.so
*.o
*.a
*.db
*.db-shm
*.db-wal
vendor/
*.tmp
*.swp
Thumbs.db

.vroom
.prds/
.private/
.claude/
.scannerwork/
bench-output.txt
api-bench-output.txt

# VitePress docs (nebula/)
nebula/.vitepress/cache/
nebula/.vitepress/dist/
